# Contributing to [[ name ]]

## Development setup

The README describes how to install [[ name ]] for development and run its checks.

## Commit messages

Commits follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org): `type(scope): description`,
with types such as `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor` and `test`.
[% if releases %]

Releases are automatic: a `feat` releases a minor version, a `fix` a patch, and a breaking change
(`type!:` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer) a major one. To force a particular release, put a
directive alone on a line in the commit body: `+:major`, `+:minor`, `+:patch`, or `+:rc` / `+:pre` /
`+:prepre` for a pre-release.
[% endif %]

## Pull requests

Keep each pull request to one change, with a Conventional Commit title and passing checks. Describe
what changed and why in the pull request itself.
